# Git
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# Python bytecode & caches
#
# `**/` IS REQUIRED and its absence is not cosmetic: Docker anchors these
# patterns at the context root and `*` does not cross `/`, so a bare
# `__pycache__` excludes only a TOP-LEVEL one. Measured on the image this file
# governs: 15 __pycache__ directories and 63 .pyc files shipped, including
# bytecode for scripts the API never runs.
#
# Two consequences. The image stops being a function of the git tree - it
# carries whatever the developer last executed - and any local pytest run
# changes the COPY layer, busting the build cache with no source change.
#
# The sibling annexes ship the byte-identical file and have the same bug.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/*.pyd
*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.pyre
.pytype
cython_debug

# Local env files (compose injects vars)
.env
.env.local
.env.production
.env.staging
.env.test

